<div class="container">
    <h1>AI in Application Development — Security, Code Quality, Consistency &amp; Checks</h1>

    <div class="last-updated">
        Status: 📋 DRAFT sub-project plan for the AI Chat / AI Development workstream.
        Intended to become a sub-project under the AI development project (parent ~114, "AI Chat Integration").
        Purpose: define HOW we use AI to write and review Comserv2 code without regressing quality or security.
    </div>

    <h2 id="now">Now (2026-10-14)</h2>
    <p><strong>Current.</strong> Aikido is installed on this host (<code>aikido-local-scanner</code>) but it is not on the commit path. Its only command is a secrets scan. The live hook is still perl -c plus gitleaks. Aikido does not score a diff for accuracy, security, or effectiveness.</p>
    <p><strong>Approved, partly built on this worktree only</strong> (<code>/home/shanta/.comserv/worktrees/aisystem/Comserv</code>, port 4006). Not on main. Not committed.</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Done in code: <code>CodeReviewer.pm</code> can store a score row, block a high finding (security below 4 or accuracy below 3), and ask <code>deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro</code> for a preview diff. It does not write files itself. <code>data/ai_reviewer.json</code> is <code>mode: block</code>, cap $0.50/day. Reviewer stays Sonnet 5.5, backup GPT-6 Sol. <code>Util/Git.pm</code> can apply a checked patch. <code>Admin/Git.pm</code> no longer commits from the form buttons until a review is confirmed.</li>
        <li>Not done: the commit page does not yet show the scores, Confirm, override, or Ask fixer. A duplicate <code>=head2 execute_git_commit</code> was left above the real method. The eval scorecard does not read the score file. <code>perl -c</code> was not run after the last edit. Do not treat <code>/admin/git_commit</code> on :4006 as a finished gate.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Working checklist (not a served page): <code>/home/shanta/PycharmProjects/comserv2/.hermes/plans/2026-10-14_061800-code-diff-review.md</code>.</p>

    <h2>1. Why this sub-project exists</h2>
    <p>We already use AI heavily: Ollama chat open to all roles, autonomous delegates (claude-code / codex /
    opencode), and the evaluator+editor pattern (cheap model plans, better model executes). The BrightTALK talk
    "From AI Experiments to Production" (Coder) names the failure modes we must guard: weak guardrails, no
    workspace isolation, ungoverned context, and no quality gates. This plan codifies our answers.</p>

    <h2>2. The gates we already have (baseline)</h2>
    <table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse;">
        <tr style="background-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.15);">
            <th style="text-align:left; padding:8px; border:1px solid var(--border-color);">Gate</th>
            <th style="text-align:left; padding:8px; border:1px solid var(--border-color);">What it catches</th>
            <th style="text-align:left; padding:8px; border:1px solid var(--border-color);">File</th>
        </tr>
        <tr><td style="padding:8px; border:1px solid var(--border-color);">Perl compile check</td>
            <td style="padding:8px; border:1px solid var(--border-color);">Random syntax errors at commit</td>
            <td style="padding:8px; border:1px solid var(--border-color);">.git/hooks/pre-commit (perl -c)</td></tr>
        <tr><td style="padding:8px; border:1px solid var(--border-color);">Secrets scan</td>
            <td style="padding:8px; border:1px solid var(--border-color);">Leaked credentials in history</td>
            <td style="padding:8px; border:1px solid var(--border-color);">pre-commit (gitleaks) + deploy (security_scan.sh)</td></tr>
        <tr><td style="padding:8px; border:1px solid var(--border-color);">Test gate</td>
            <td style="padding:8px; border:1px solid var(--border-color);">Logic regressions before merge</td>
            <td style="padding:8px; border:1px solid var(--border-color);">script/test_gate.sh (pre-merge)</td></tr>
        <tr><td style="padding:8px; border:1px solid var(--border-color);">Security scan</td>
            <td style="padding:8px; border:1px solid var(--border-color);">CPAN/trivy/gitleaks on deploy</td>
            <td style="padding:8px; border:1px solid var(--border-color);">deploy.sh COMSERV_SECURITY_GATE=1</td></tr>
        <tr><td style="padding:8px; border:1px solid var(--border-color);">Whitelisted git runner</td>
            <td style="padding:8px; border:1px solid var(--border-color);">Shell-injection via git ops</td>
            <td style="padding:8px; border:1px solid var(--border-color);">Comserv::Util::Git</td></tr>
        <tr><td style="padding:8px; border:1px solid var(--border-color);">Schema-compare only</td>
            <td style="padding:8px; border:1px solid var(--border-color);">AI bypassing DB schema API</td>
            <td style="padding:8px; border:1px solid var(--border-color);">.ai-policy.md §5</td></tr>
    </table>

    <h2>3. Consistency rules the AI must obey</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>File size targets</strong> (Controllers &le;2000 soft / 4000 hard; Util/Model/Result &le;800 / 1500;
            templates &le;1000 / 2000) — from .ai-policy.md §1.</li>
        <li><strong>Naming:</strong> PascalCase packages/classes, snake_case DB columns/fields.</li>
        <li><strong>Catalyst structure:</strong> heavy logic in <code>Comserv::Util::*</code> /
            <code>Comserv::Model::*</code>; Result classes are the single source of truth for columns.</li>
        <li><strong>JS migration:</strong> no inline &lt;script&gt; in js_load.tt templates; extend existing modules
            under <code>static/js/</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>Theme:</strong> only <code>var(--*)</code> colours and existing component classes.</li>
        <li><strong>Logging:</strong> full <code>log_with_details($c, LEVEL, __FILE__, __LINE__, ...)</code> during
            active development.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Human-in-the-loop (the hard gate)</h2>
    <p>Per standing policy, the agent WAITS indefinitely for an explicit answer on any decision — it never
    auto-picks a default. Schema changes go through the in-app schema-compare workflow (a human action). The
    agent does not commit/push/deploy without being asked. This is our primary guardrail and must remain
    non-negotiable even as automation grows.</p>

    <h2>5. Workspace isolation (extends dev_isolation_and_backups_plan.tt)</h2>
    <p>Feature branches already run in git worktrees (zenflow) with their own server instance. The remaining
    gap is <strong>database isolation</strong>: worktree agents currently resolve to production. The companion
    plan forces <code>ACTIVE_DB_ENVIRONMENT=dev</code> for any non-main instance so AI agents can never mutate
    live data. This sub-project owns the <em>policy</em>; the companion plan owns the <em>mechanism</em>.</p>

    <h2>6. How we "check" AI output (the loop)</h2>
    <ol>
        <li><strong>Plan (cheap model):</strong> propose the change against the existing gates above.</li>
        <li><strong>Execute (better model / delegate):</strong> implement, confined to task scope.</li>
        <li><strong>Self-check:</strong> pre-commit hook (compile + secrets) runs automatically on a terminal <code>git commit</code>. That hook does not call Aikido and does not call the model reviewer.</li>
        <li><strong>Diff review (this worktree, unfinished):</strong> the app commit form is supposed to score accuracy, security, and effectiveness with a model that did not write the diff, then refuse a high finding unless an admin overrides with a reason. A third model may propose a preview. Nothing is written until Apply. This is not live yet. See the Now section.</li>
        <li><strong>Gate:</strong> agent runs <code>script/test_gate.sh</code> before reporting done; must be green.</li>
        <li><strong>Review:</strong> human merges to main; deploy runs the security scan when
            <code>COMSERV_SECURITY_GATE=1</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>Audit:</strong> every error &rarr; todo &rarr; email pipeline already records regressions for
            follow-up.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>7. Gaps to close (roadmap)</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Make <code>test_gate.sh</code> the default pre-merge step in the agent workflow (not opt-in).</li>
        <li>Run <code>perlcritic</code> on changed <code>.pm</code> in pre-commit (configurable severity).</li>
        <li>Enforce <code>COMSERV_SECURITY_GATE=1</code> on production deploys by default.</li>
        <li>Wire dev-DB isolation (companion plan) so agent runs are prod-safe by construction.</li>
        <li>Finish the commit-form review (template, remove the duplicate POD, <code>perl -c</code>, then the eval score column). Do not copy it to main until that gate works on :4006.</li>
    </ul>

    <p style="margin-top:20px;"><em>Next: promote to a sub-project (parent ~114), then implement the §7 roadmap items
    incrementally, each behind the §6 loop.</em></p>
</div>
